Fixes https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/150550.

With the test case 
```
void f(unsigned char *x, unsigned char *y, int n) {
  // should have been vectorized into avgr_u instead of seperated vectorized add and logical right shift
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    x[i] = (x[i] + y[i] + 1) / 2;
}
```

the backend failed to recognize that this can be reduced to avgr_u since the loop vectorizer doesn't transform into the existing pattern in tablegen. 

This PR sets AVGCEIL_U as legal for v8i16 and v16i8 and selects it to avgr_u in the tablegen file.

This PR fixes a critical issue where import atoms would become permanently broken when referencing files that were uploaded but never committed to the repository.

## Problem

When a user uploads a file to an import atom but doesn't save the project, the following sequence occurs:

1. File is uploaded and `fileName` is set in the import atom
2. File is uploaded to GitHub repository temporarily
3. Project is not saved, so the file is never committed
4. Next time the project loads, `beginPropagation()` calls `updateValue()` 
5. `updateValue()` tries to fetch the non-existent file via `getAFile()`
6. The GitHub API returns a 404 error, but there was no error handling
7. Import atom remains in a broken state with a filename that can't be resolved

## Solution

Added comprehensive error handling to the `updateValue()` method in the import atom:

```javascript
this.getAFile().then((result) => {
  // ... existing success handling
}).catch((error) => {
  // Handle file not found error - reset atom state to allow re-upload
  if (error.status === 404) {
    console.log(`File not found in repository: ${this.fileName}. Resetting import atom to allow re-upload.`);
    this.fileName = null;
    this.type = null;
    this.sha = null;
    this.processing = false;
  } else {
    // For other errors, show error message but don't reset state
    console.error(`Error retrieving file: ${error.message || error}`);
    if (typeof alert !== 'undefined') {
      alert(`Error retrieving file: ${error.message || error}`);
    }
    this.processing = false;
  }
});
```

## Key Features

- **Smart Error Differentiation**: Only resets atom state for 404 (file not found) errors
- **Graceful Recovery**: Allows users to upload a new file when the previous one is missing
- **Preserved State**: Maintains atom state for other error types (network issues, permissions, etc.)
- **Cross-Environment Compatibility**: Alert calls are conditional to work in both browser and test environments
- **Comprehensive Testing**: Added full test suite covering all error scenarios

## Testing

- Added 5 new test cases covering the fix behavior
- All existing tests continue to pass (52/52 total)
- Verified build process and development server functionality
- Manual testing confirms import atoms properly reset when files are missing

Fixes #726.

